# VoiceVision External Integrations
# Source: integrations/

## Home Assistant (integrations/homeassistant/)
- Custom component in custom_components/voicevision/
- Config flow: base_url, token, timeout
- Services: voicevision.converse, voicevision.transcribe, voicevision.describe
- Events: voicevision_response fired with {service, text/audio_file/image_file, response/transcript/description}
- Not tested in CI (Home Assistant not installed) - structural validation only
- Runs in executor (hass.async_add_executor_job)

## VS Code (integrations/vscode/)
- Plain CommonJS extension.js (no build step, no node_modules)
- Commands: voicevision.dictate, voicevision.transcribeFile, voicevision.ask
- Dictate: shells out to voicevision-listen --quiet
- Transcribe/Ask: POST to local HTTP server
- Settings: serverUrl, token, language, listenCommand, listenArgs, maxTokens
- Errors → showErrorMessage notifications
- node --check validates extension.js

## Obsidian (integrations/obsidian/)
- Desktop-only plugin (isDesktopOnly: true)
- Commands: transcribe-audio-file, ask-about-selection
- Settings tab: serverUrl, token, language, maxTokens
- Transcribe: PathModal for WAV file path → POST /transcribe
- Ask: editor.replaceSelection with /converse response
- Uses Obsidian's requestUrl (bypasses CORS)
- Mobile not supported (no fs access)

## Notion (integrations/notion/)
- voicevision_notion.py CLI
- Transcribes locally (--audio) or uses existing text (--text-file)
- Creates Notion page under parent page (--page-id) or database (--database-id)
- Blocks split at 2000 chars (prefers newline, then space, then hard cut)
- Token from NOTION_TOKEN env var (only at export time, never logged)
- --dry-run prints payload without contacting Notion
- Inference stays local; Notion export is explicit opt-in cloud step